    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Meet Frank and Percy, an unlikely pair, who strike up a friendship while dog walking on Hampstead Heath. Soon enough, their platonic bond quietly blossoms into something far more tender. Featuring a star-studded ensemble including Stephen Fry, Joanna Lumley, Derek Jacobi, Ncuti Gatwa and Siân Phillips, this charming tale of late-blooming love is a warm-hearted and soul-searching gem."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Wema Mumma"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "How to book"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Tickets start from £10 for all screenings and events in London, with concessions available for many screenings. Booking information and ticket prices .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Booking information and ticket prices",
          "url": "https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=tickets-booking-information"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For non-Members we charge £1 per ticket for online and phone bookings, up to £3 per transaction. There’s no booking fee if you buy tickets at the box office."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If you’re aged 16 to 25, sign up for free to BFI 25 and Under for a chance to get £6 tickets (without booking fees) to all screenings and events, subject to availability.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "BFI 25 and Under",
          "url": "https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=25-and-under-lff"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Missed out?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "More tickets may become available for these screenings before and during the festival. Find out about extra ticket releases and standby queues .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Find out about extra ticket releases and standby queues",
          "url": "https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=tickets-booking-information#extra-ticket-releases"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Our programmers recommend..."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/elsinore-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Elsinore"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Andrew Scott is a towering presence in this singular account of Ian Charleson’s life, capturing the moment when he faced his own mortality as he prepared to play Hamlet at the Royal National Theatre."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/idiots-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The Idiot(s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Aimee Lou Wood and Johnny Flynn are superb as Anna and Fyodor Dostoevsky in Małgorzata Szumowska and Michał Englert’s acerbic and joyful period film."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/ha-chan-shake-your-booty-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Ha-Chan, Shake Your Booty!"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Recently widowed Haru rediscovers her love for ballroom dancing, only to find herself attracted to her new instructor, in this zany, toe-tapping film."
    }
  ]
